.TH MINWIN 1 "September 2026" "minwin 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
minwin \- minimal fullscreen terminal window manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minwin
.RB [ \-c " key" ]
.RB [ \-s ]
.RI [ command " [" argument " ...]]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minwin
runs multiple independent pseudo-terminals in one terminal and displays one
at a time. It provides windows but no split panes and no session server.
Run it under
.BR abduco (1)
for persistent attach/detach sessions, and run
.BR mtm (1)
inside a window when split panes are needed.
.PP
One row is reserved for a window list unless disabled with
.BR \-s .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " key"
Set the command prefix. The argument may be a literal character, caret notation
such as
.BR ^G ,
or a decimal byte value.
.TP
.B \-s
Hide the status line and give every row to the child terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h , " --help"
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B --self-test
Run the internal VT-model tests and exit.
.SH KEYS
Commands use
.B Ctrl-a
by default.
.TP
.B c
Create a shell window.
.TP
.B m
Create a window running mtm, or the command named by MINWIN_MTM.
.TP
.BR n , " p"
Select the next or previous window.
.TP
.BR 1\-9 , " 0"
Select window 1 through 10.
.TP
.B x
Send SIGHUP to the current window's process group and close it.
.TP
.B l
Redraw the screen.
.TP
.B ?
Display the key summary until another key is pressed.
.TP
.B Ctrl-a
When entered after the prefix, send a literal Ctrl-a to the application.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
Shell used for new windows. The user's login shell and /bin/sh are fallbacks.
.TP
.B MINWIN_MTM
Program started by the
.B m
command. The default is mtm.
.TP
.B TERM
Describes the hosting terminal. Child terminals receive screen-256color by
default; this is configurable in config.h.
.SH PERSISTENCE
For a persistent workspace, use:
.PP
.RS
.B abduco -A main minwin
.RE
.PP
The default abduco detach key is Ctrl-backslash. Minwin keeps its child PTYs
drained while detached and redraws on terminal resize or with its redraw key.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Minwin has no scrollback, copy mode, detach protocol, split layout, or plugin
system. OSC clipboard and hyperlink sequences and graphical terminal protocols
are not passed through.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR abduco (1),
.BR mtm (1),
.BR pty (7)
